We want to find the smallest positive integer $n$ such that $n > 1$ and $n$ is relatively prime to $20!$.
Since $20! = 2^4 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdot 11 \cdot 13 \cdot 17 \cdot 19$, we need to find the smallest integer greater than 1 that is not divisible by any of these primes.
In other words, we need to find the smallest integer greater than 1 that is not divisible by 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, or 19.

