If $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are even functions, then $-f(x)$ and $-g(x)$ are also even functions.
Let $h(x) = f(x) \cdot g(x)$.
Since $f(x)$ is an even function, $f(-x) = f(x)$.
Since $g(x)$ is an even function, $g(-x) = g(x)$.
Then $h(-x) = f(-x) \cdot g(-x) = f(x) \cdot g(x) = h(x)$.
Therefore, $h(x)$ is an even function.

\boxed{even}
