We have $100 = p_1 + p_2$, so $p_2 = 100 - p_1$. We test the possible values of $p_1$:
\begin{itemize}
\item $p_1=2$. Then $p_2 = 100 - 2 = 98$, which is not prime.
\item $p_1=3$. Then $p_2 = 100 - 3 = 97$, which is prime.
\item $p_1=5$. Then $p_2 = 100 - 5 = 95$, which is not prime, because $95 = 5 \cdot 19$.
\item $p_1=7$. Then $p_2 = 100 - 7 = 93$, which is not prime, because $93 = 3 \cdot 31$.
\end{itemize}
Therefore, $p_1 = 3$ and $p_2 = 97$. The product of these prime numbers is $3 \cdot 97 = 291$.

