\boxed{ 54 \text{ square meters } }
The volume of a cube is given by the formula $V = s^3$, where $V$ is the volume and $s$ is the side length.
Given that the volume is $V = 0.027$ cubic meters, we can find the side length $s$ by solving $s^3 = 0.027$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{0.027} = 0.3$ meters.
The surface area of a cube is given by the formula $A = 6s^2$, where $A$ is the surface area and $s$ is the side length.
Substituting $s = 0.3$ into the formula, we get $A = 6(0.3)^2 = 6(0.09) = 0.54$ square meters.

\boxed{0.54 \text{ square meters } }
